{%- comment -%}
  Pixel dissolve — the transition out of a full-bleed colour block.

  WHY THIS EXISTS RATHER THAN gc2-edge. That snippet draws coloured teeth on
  transparency and sits BELOW the block it closes, so its flat fill has to match
  whatever is above it. Against the hero it does not: the hero's pink is a huge
  radial gradient, so a flat cherry band met it in a hard horizontal seam, and
  the shape read as bunting rather than as the book's stepped border.

  This inverts the whole idea. It draws the PAGE colour, and it sits ON TOP of
  the block's last stretch. So the colour above every gap is the block's own —
  gradient, photo, whatever — and the colour of the teeth is the page's own.
  There is no seam to match because nothing is being matched: both halves are
  the real thing showing through a stencil.

  The motif itself is squares on a fixed grid, never triangles: a stepped
  pyramid rising out of a solid base, then detached pixels floating clear of it,
  so the block looks like it is breaking up into the page rather than being cut
  off by a border.

  Params:
    id    (required) unique per instance. Pattern ids collide otherwise, and a
          duplicate silently makes every later band reuse the first one.
          MUST be pre-assigned — {% render %} does not evaluate filters.
    tone  colour token for the TEETH — the page behind, not the block above.
          Default '--c-bg'.
    scale size of one pixel. 1 = 10px. Default 0.8, giving 8px pixels and a
          128px band, which reads as deliberate on a phone and on a laptop.

  Usage:
    {%- assign did = 'hero-out' -%}
    {% render 'gc2-dissolve', id: did, tone: '--c-bg' %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign tone  = tone  | default: '--c-bg' -%}
{%- assign scale = scale | default: 0.8 -%}
{%- comment -%}
  A SECOND scale, for phones. The tile is 120x160 cells, so at 0.8 it is 96px
  wide — eleven across a laptop and barely four across a 390px phone. Four is
  not a dissolve, it is four lumps, and that is how it read. The comment above
  claimed 0.8 "reads as deliberate on a phone"; it does not.

  0.4 gives 48px tiles, about eight across a phone, and a 64px band. The band
  height is load-bearing: .gh-edge pulls itself up by it and .gh-reveal reserves
  it, so both follow this number in section-gc-home.css.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign scale_m = scale_mobile | default: 0.4 -%}

{%- comment -%} tile is 12 x 16 cells of 10px {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign unit_w = 120 | times: scale -%}
{%- assign unit_h = 160 | times: scale -%}
{%- assign unit_wm = 120 | times: scale_m -%}
{%- assign unit_hm = 160 | times: scale_m -%}

<svg class="gc2-dissolve" width="100%"
     style="--dh:{{ unit_h }}px;--dhm:{{ unit_hm }}px"
     aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" role="presentation">
  <defs>
    <pattern id="gc2dis-{{ id }}" width="{{ unit_w }}" height="{{ unit_h }}" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
      <g transform="scale({{ scale }})" fill="var({{ tone }})">
        {%- comment -%} stepped pyramid, column heights 2 3 4 6 8 10 10 8 6 4 3 2 {%- endcomment -%}
        <rect x="0"   y="140" width="10" height="20"></rect>
        <rect x="10"  y="130" width="10" height="30"></rect>
        <rect x="20"  y="120" width="10" height="40"></rect>
        <rect x="30"  y="100" width="10" height="60"></rect>
        <rect x="40"  y="80"  width="10" height="80"></rect>
        <rect x="50"  y="60"  width="10" height="100"></rect>
        <rect x="60"  y="60"  width="10" height="100"></rect>
        <rect x="70"  y="80"  width="10" height="80"></rect>
        <rect x="80"  y="100" width="10" height="60"></rect>
        <rect x="90"  y="120" width="10" height="40"></rect>
        <rect x="100" y="130" width="10" height="30"></rect>
        <rect x="110" y="140" width="10" height="20"></rect>
        {%- comment -%} detached pixels — the block breaking up as it goes {%- endcomment -%}
        <rect x="50"  y="40"  width="10" height="10"></rect>
        <rect x="60"  y="40"  width="10" height="10"></rect>
        <rect x="60"  y="20"  width="10" height="10"></rect>
        <rect x="0"   y="110" width="10" height="10"></rect>
      </g>
    </pattern>
    <pattern id="gc2dism-{{ id }}" width="{{ unit_wm }}" height="{{ unit_hm }}" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
      <g transform="scale({{ scale_m }})" fill="var({{ tone }})">
        {%- comment -%} stepped pyramid, column heights 2 3 4 6 8 10 10 8 6 4 3 2 {%- endcomment -%}
        <rect x="0"   y="140" width="10" height="20"></rect>
        <rect x="10"  y="130" width="10" height="30"></rect>
        <rect x="20"  y="120" width="10" height="40"></rect>
        <rect x="30"  y="100" width="10" height="60"></rect>
        <rect x="40"  y="80"  width="10" height="80"></rect>
        <rect x="50"  y="60"  width="10" height="100"></rect>
        <rect x="60"  y="60"  width="10" height="100"></rect>
        <rect x="70"  y="80"  width="10" height="80"></rect>
        <rect x="80"  y="100" width="10" height="60"></rect>
        <rect x="90"  y="120" width="10" height="40"></rect>
        <rect x="100" y="130" width="10" height="30"></rect>
        <rect x="110" y="140" width="10" height="20"></rect>
        {%- comment -%} detached pixels — the block breaking up as it goes {%- endcomment -%}
        <rect x="50"  y="40"  width="10" height="10"></rect>
        <rect x="60"  y="40"  width="10" height="10"></rect>
        <rect x="60"  y="20"  width="10" height="10"></rect>
        <rect x="0"   y="110" width="10" height="10"></rect>
      </g>
    </pattern>
  </defs>
  <rect class="gc2-dissolve__wide" width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#gc2dis-{{ id }})"></rect>
  <rect class="gc2-dissolve__fine" width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#gc2dism-{{ id }})"></rect>
</svg>
